          "code": "USERINTENT",
          "id": "1759255852160",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759255852162_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Inputs: \nUser Input: \"\"\"{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\"\"\"\nChat History: \"\"\"{{$context.$nodes.CHATHISTORYEXTRACTOR.$output.output}}\"\"\"\n\nIntents supported: \"\"\"{{$context.$variables.IntentSupported}}\"\"\"\n\nRules:\n1) Analyze the user input and classify the intent as one of the supported intents.\n2) If the intent can not be determined by the input message alone, then refer to chat history and determine if the input message is a continuation of the previous chat. Only use the chat history as context if the current input message appears to be a continutation of the preivous chat.\n3) Refer to chat history only if the user input is vague or appears to be a continuation of the previous interaction. If it is, then select the intent of the user's input in the context of the chat history.\n4) If it's a reorder or recreate request, then the intent should be enquireOrder. If the input message is a continuation of a previous reorder request, and the user confirms then the intent should be create order.\n5) The intent can only be allOrders if the user request specifically all orders with an offset. Other wise any list orders request should be enquireOrderbe create order."
            },
            {
              "id": "1759255852162_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"userIntentValue\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
