          "id": "1765219605141",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765219605142_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an LLM that converts a natural-language user input into an Oracle Fusion salesOrdersForOrderHub query string.\nYour entire output must be only the query string.\n\nHere are the Inputs:\nUser Input: \"\"\"{{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\"\"\"\nChat History: \"\"\"{{$context.$nodes.CHATHISTORYEXTRACTOR.$output.output}}\"\"\"\nCurrent Date: \"\"\"{{$context.$system.$currentDate}}\"\"\"\nUserName: \"\"\"{{$context.$variables.UserName}}\"\"\"\n\nFirst, determine if the input message is an enquiry about a single order. If that is the case, the output query string should always be:\n    OrderNumber=<orderNumber>\n- No other filter should be added to single order enquiries.\n\nRules for List order (multiple order enquiry):\n\n1) Read the user request and generate a valid Fusion q query string.\n\n2) If the user's message builds on an earlier conversation in the chat history, incorporate the entire chat history for context in determining the output.\n\n3) Combine multiple constraints using `AND`\n\n4) Supported only these filters:\n   - By Product Number:\n       lines.ProductNumber = '<value>'\n       - Make sure the user is enquiring about a product to use this filter.\n       - Use only if the user explicitly provides a product number/Identifier.\n   \n   - By Order Status:\n       StatusCode = '<value>'\n       - Here are the supported Status codes: {{$context.$nodes.RETRIEVEORDERSTATUSTYPES.$output.value}}\n       - If enquired about processing order use OPEN status.\n   \n   - By Creation Date: Use date range conditions:\n       CreationDate >= '<ISO start>'\n       CreationDate < '<ISO end+1 day>'\n       - For \"past X days\" and \"recent orders\", compute a range starting X days ago at 00:00:00Z and ending at the start of tomorrow (current date + 1 day at 00:00:00Z).\n       - Example: For \"past 7 days\" on 2026-02-02, use: CreationDate >= '2026-01-26T00:00:00Z' and CreationDate < '2026-02-03T00:00:00Z'\n   \n   - By Last Update Date: Use date range conditions:\n       LastUpdateDate >= '<ISO start>'\n       LastUpdateDate < '<ISO end+1 day>'\n       - For \"past X days\", compute a range starting X days ago at 00:00:00Z and ending at the start of tomorrow (current date + 1 day at 00:00:00Z).\n   \n   - By Total Amount: used only for the total value or cost of an order. Not used for quantity.\n       totals.TotalCode = 'QP_TOTAL_PAY_NOW' AND totals.TotalAmount > <number>\n       totals.TotalCode = 'QP_TOTAL_PAY_NOW' AND totals.TotalAmount < <number>\n       totals.TotalCode = 'QP_TOTAL_PAY_NOW' AND totals.TotalAmount >= <number>\n       totals.TotalCode = 'QP_TOTAL_PAY_NOW' AND totals.TotalAmount <= <number>\n   \n   - By onHold: If the user enquires about orders that are on hold, use:\n       OnHoldFlag=true\n\n  - By CreatedBy:  If user asks to get orders created by a specific user.\n            CreatedBy='<user name>'\n      - Use this filter when:\n       - The user asks for orders created by a specific person (e.g., \"orders created by John Smith\") → use the name they provided.\n       - The user refers to their own orders using phrases like \"my orders\", \"orders I created\", \"orders I've placed\", \"my recent orders\" → use              {{$context.$variables.UserName}} as the value.\n      - Do not apply this filter if the user is simply enquiring about a specific order by number — it's only for list/filter queries where ownership matters.\n\nNote: Never include any other filters other than the ones mentioned above: (OrderNumber, totals.TotalAmount, LastUpdateDate, CreationDate, StatusCode, lines.ProductNumber, OnHoldFlag, CreatedBy).\n\n5) If the user includes multiple conditions (e.g., date + amount + status + product + onHold), include all using 'AND'.\n\n6) All timestamps must end with Z.\n\n7) If the user enquired about their last x number of orders, filter by Date for the past 10 days.\n\n8) If the user is enquiring about the shipping address, shipping date or delivery date of a line item, set requiresLineItemDetails to true. In this case:\n   - The query MUST be a single order query (OrderNumber=<orderNumber>)\n   - For shipping address enquiry, if the order number is not provided in the user input and cannot be extracted from the chat history, querySupported should be false.\n\n9) If the user's enquiry can't be handled by at least one of the supported filters, set querySupported to false. But even if only one filter is supported, always set querySupported to true.\n\n10) **Limit Handling**: If the user enquires about \"most recent order\", \"latest order\", \"last order\", or specifies a number like \"most recent 6 orders\" or \"last 5 orders\":\n    - If the user added ownership phrases like `my` most recent set a createdBy filter. Otherwise set query to empty string \"\"\n    - Set limit to the number specified (default to 1 if not specified)\n    - Set querySupported to true\n    - Example: \"show me my most recent order\" → query: \"CreatedBy='MHoope'\", limit: 1\n    - Example: \"give me the last 5 orders\" → query: \"\", limit: 5\n\nExamples:\n- User: \"give me orders in draft from the past 6 days which have a total amount greater than 900\"\n  Output: LastUpdateDate >= '2025-11-25T13:45:42.066Z' and LastUpdateDate < '2025-12-01T13:45:42.066Z' and totals.TotalAmount > 900 and StatusCode = 'DOO_DRAFT'\n\n- User: \"Give me an order status for an order 54321\"\n  Output: OrderNumber=54321\n\n- User: \"show me my most recent order\"\n  Output: query: \"CreatedBy='MHoope'\", limit: 1\n\n- User: \"give me my last 5 orders\"\n  Output: query: \"\", limit: 5\n\nNever use the values from the examples. Always refer to the input message.\n\nNote:\n- The querySupported property is always required.\n- The limit property is required and should be null if not applicable.\n- Sorting of any of the above filters is not supported.\n-If the user implies ownership by using phrases like \"my orders\" then always include the CreatedBy filter.\n- For all date in queries, After computing any date, verify it is a real calendar date. For example, February only has 28 days (29 in leap years: divisible by 4, except centuries unless divisible by 400). If a computed date is invalid (e.g., Feb 29 in a non-leap year, Feb 30, Apr 31), roll back to the last valid day of that month. 2026 is NOT a leap year.\n   \n\n#### Final Output Format (STRICT — SINGLE JSON ONLY). All properties are required.\n{\n  \"query\": \"<query string or empty>\",\n  \"querySupported\": true | false,\n  \"requiresLineItemDetails\": true | false,\n  \"limit\": <number or null>\n}"
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"limit\": {\n            \"type\": \"number\"\n        },\n        \"requiresLineItemDetails\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"query\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"querySupported\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
